      "edits": [
        {
          "mode": "insert_before",
          "anchor": "<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Was Matsue Vogel Park worth it?</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->",
          "fragment": "<!-- tsurikue-en-san-in-vogel-20261113 -->\n<!-- wp:heading -->\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Make it a San'in road trip, if you have more time</h2>\n<!-- /wp:heading -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Matsue Vogel Park is easy to visit by train, and you don't need a car just to see the birds. But if you're exploring more of Shimane and Tottori, a car makes it easier to follow a scenic detour whenever something catches your eye.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>Around Matsue, there's <strong>Lake Shinji</strong> for lakeside scenery, <strong>GOBIUS</strong> for freshwater creatures, <strong>Tamatsukuri Onsen</strong> for a hot-spring stop, and <strong>Matsue Castle</strong> for a change of pace. With extra time, you could continue to <strong>Sakaiminato</strong> for its yokai-filled streets or drive toward <strong>Mount Daisen</strong> for mountain views.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>That's a menu of places for a wider trip, not a checklist to squeeze into one day. The park itself kept us busy for around five hours!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p>If a road trip sounds like your kind of adventure, you can <a href=\"https://www.discovercars.com/?a_aid=tsurikue\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"sponsored nofollow noopener\"><strong>compare rental car options in Japan</strong></a> before deciding. For a simple visit to Vogel Park, the train is still a great choice.</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n\n<!-- wp:paragraph -->\n<p><strong>A Small Note from Me 🚗</strong> This is an affiliate link. If you book through it, I may earn a commission. It helps me keep exploring Hiroshima and sharing firsthand travel experiences. Thanks for reading!</p>\n<!-- /wp:paragraph -->\n"
        }
      ]
    }
